  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.24,
      "end_seconds": 5.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I've settled them in, ready when you are."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.49,
      "end_seconds": 10.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Okay thanks. Hi how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.45,
      "end_seconds": 17.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Um so... a painful ulcer that is growing quickly. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.43,
      "end_seconds": 22.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.57,
      "end_seconds": 31.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "about... well three days my family kept telling me to get it checked"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.56,
      "end_seconds": 43.49,
      "duration_seconds": 11.93,
      "text": "Yes. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.04,
      "end_seconds": 70.55,
      "duration_seconds": 25.51,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day. I'd say mild. Oh, and belly cramps and loose stools. That's been about the same, three days. As for belly cramps and loose stools, I'd say mild. Oh, and starting as a pimple. That's been about the same, about two weeks. With starting as a pimple, mostly severe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.53,
      "end_seconds": 86.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.42,
      "end_seconds": 91.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "my uncle has high cholesterol"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.02,
      "end_seconds": 97.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.95,
      "end_seconds": 101.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "not to my knowledge, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.72,
      "end_seconds": 117.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "right, what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.64,
      "end_seconds": 128.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "I'm on febuxostat, 80 milligrams, maybe, once a day for the gout"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.12,
      "end_seconds": 133.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.32,
      "end_seconds": 138.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "no you know it's at home"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.74,
      "end_seconds": 152.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.58,
      "end_seconds": 156.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.05,
      "end_seconds": 160.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.09,
      "end_seconds": 164.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.68,
      "end_seconds": 170.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.02,
      "end_seconds": 174.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.19,
      "end_seconds": 179.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.79,
      "end_seconds": 187.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "So, I had a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.04,
      "end_seconds": 190.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.34,
      "end_seconds": 192.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Yes gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.34,
      "end_seconds": 198.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "have you noticed diabetes, recent cut or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.31,
      "end_seconds": 202.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "no, I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.76,
      "end_seconds": 207.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Did you notice any recent injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.84,
      "end_seconds": 210.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "nope, no recent injury"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.9,
      "end_seconds": 214.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.33,
      "end_seconds": 220.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "breathing's normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.01,
      "end_seconds": 224.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "any trouble with the the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.05,
      "end_seconds": 227.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "no, that's all fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 229.1,
      "end_seconds": 238.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pressure 111 over 71, saturation 97 percent, temp 36.5 degrees. Pulse is 70 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.62,
      "end_seconds": 239.53,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.35,
      "end_seconds": 246.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second make yourself comfortable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.14,
      "end_seconds": 249.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Yeah no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.8,
      "end_seconds": 253.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.58,
      "end_seconds": 271.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "the ulcer has a ragged purple edge with a boggy base and undermined borders"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.55,
      "end_seconds": 273.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "okay, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.7,
      "end_seconds": 289.79,
      "duration_seconds": 14.09,
      "text": "Okay, good, you can sit up again. From what you've told me and what I found, this is probably possible pyoderma gangrenosum linked to bowel inflammation. I can't rule out an infected ulcer yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.55,
      "end_seconds": 295.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.88,
      "end_seconds": 318.72,
      "duration_seconds": 21.84,
      "text": "I can't promise yet but most people with possible pyoderma gangrenosum linked to bowel inflammation do well once it's treated properly. Let's book blood tests to look into ulcer. I'm going to order a stool test for bowel symptoms. Do not cut or scrub it that can make it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.24,
      "end_seconds": 349.14,
      "duration_seconds": 29.9,
      "text": "I follow i'd like you to see the dermatology clinic as well, and I'll write the referral and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose if the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department see me again after the biopsy that's everything on my side anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.41,
      "end_seconds": 353.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.82,
      "end_seconds": 357.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "all the best"
    }
  ]
